The preload needs to be chosen so that the sample only deforms elastically during the phase when it is not yet being heated. To ensure accurate LME evaluation, the goal is to prevent failures caused purely by mechanical overload and instead focus on temperature-dependent material changes. Hence, the force to preload the sample must be chosen within a range that initially causes only elastic deformation before the temperature increase and then leads to an increasingly larger plastic portion as heating progresses. The formula used to estimate the tensile load is preload < yield strength at room tempearture * cross section area \documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
