Key values should allow an analysis of results without the use of absolute values rather than relative ones for a quick assessment of the LME susceptibility. As there is no standardized procedure for assessing a materials’ LME susceptibility using the CLT, a key value had to be selected carefully. The HTT according to VDA guideline provided a useful reference, offering insights on relevant metrics and their interpretation. Similarly, the relative differences between coated and uncoated samples were chosen as the primary evaluation criteria. The sample fracture elongation dependent on the preload was identified as a meaningful parameter for analysis. The relative values were calculated using the following formula. Δ fracture elongation % = fracture elongation coated - fracture elongation uncoated [ fracture elongation uncoated ] * 100 \documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
